    narr:generatedFrom "88e36c162aa3ba30a94074c3b2f7b68fbe13aefc" ;
    narr:narration """Xavier's voice here is an expert's, and it moves across three settings. In the weekly thread he [invites the steering group's push before it lands](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_10), argues [pairing two sites through a shared dispatch desk](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_12), and [flags the thinness of his own evidence](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_21). He sets [a replica-only rule during cutover](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_26), grounded in [a past outage under load](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_24) and priced against [a replica-lag range](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_28); a second thread runs from [an open question on reference-data ownership](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_34) to [a vendor-stays-system-of-record position](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_36) argued via [drift between sites](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_38). A week later he [ranks competing arguments for the same rule](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_15), offers [a learning-curve rationale](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_19), and [names a shared unstated assumption](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_25); he also [endorses a shortened window while pricing its cost](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_13) and [puts its tightness on the record](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_15). Newest, a legacy-archive thread: he [rejects keeping the old platform alive](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_7), argues [extracting closed history into a self-describing archive](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_9), insists [the meaning is what rots](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_13), names [why the argument never gets done](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_15), and [commits to a deadline](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_28).""" ;
